     "result_text_tail": "ved the storyline myself.\n- I read the ambition as \"$40M of revenue in 2030\".\n- I treated one-time costs as expenses in the year incurred.\n- I modelled inventory as four months of landed cost, as the pack specifies.\n\n**Changes after an independent challenge of the recommendation**\n\nIt confirmed all my numbers and led to three changes:\n- \"Only route that fits the limits\" became \"only route that builds a sizeable US business\", because Japan also fits.\n- The 2032 date for $40M is labelled as an extension of the plan's last year, not a forecast.\n- The cash slide now notes that the plan counts full-year 2027 sales although the decision comes in March. A six-month delay leaves cash near zero by 2030.\n\n**Checks**\n- **Sourcing:** every one of the 205 numbers comes from the briefing pack or is calculated from it, with a live formula in the workbook. No placeholders remain.\n- **QA:** the checker shows no failures and one warning. That warning flags the 28.6% break-even on the ad-cost slide as not computed from its chart; it is computed in that slide's own calculation strip, so I left it.\n- **Layout:** the renderer reports no layout problems. I couldn't look at the slides visually because the sandbox blocked Quick Look, so please flip through the deck once in PowerPoint.\n\nThe deck has 21 slides, 14 of them content slides. The spec and the script that builds it are in `work/` if you want to change anything.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx"
    }
